+# The rules
+
+Every rule below is written so it can fail. "Make it clear" is not a rule; "a money value carries
+an explicit sign" is. Where a rule is mechanically checkable it names the check.
+
+## Money
+
+**M1. Absence is an em dash, never a zero.**
+A value that was not measured renders `—`. `0.00` asserts a fact that was never established, which
+in a billing product is a false statement about money. `null`, `undefined`, `''` and unparseable
+input all render `—`. A real `0` is not absence and renders `0.00`.
+*Fails if:* any formatting path returns `0`, `0.00` or `''` for a nullish input. Asserted in
+`tests/money_test.ts`.
+
+**M2. Money never round-trips through a float.**
+Amounts arrive as string-encoded decimals (`MoneySchemaV1`, `Decimal(18,4)`). Formatting groups and
+rounds the digits themselves. `(2.675).toFixed(2)` is `'2.67'` in JavaScript; Ledgerline renders
+`2.68`. Rounding is half-up on the decimal digits.
+*Fails if:* a display path calls `toFixed`/`Number` on an amount to produce its rendered digits.
+
+**M3. Precision is never flattened.**
+A metered unit price of `0.0015` renders `0.0015`, never `0.00`. Derived precision is at least 2 and
+at most the domain's 6; an explicit `precision` may narrow it, never silently widen it.
+
+**M4. Every amount renders with tabular numerals.**
+`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` (token `--ns-numeric-tabular`) plus the numeric font, so digits
+share a width and a column of amounts aligns on the decimal. Never proportional figures.
+
+**M5. Sign is explicit and direction is a token, not a colour literal.**
+Towards us renders `+` only where the surface asks for it (`signed`), away from us always renders
+`-`. Direction selects `--ns-money-pos` / `--ns-money-neg` / `--ns-money-flat` / `--ns-absent`
+through `moneyParts().direction`. No component re-derives "is this negative?" from a comparison.
+
+**M6. A ratio with no supportable denominator is `null`, not `0`.**
+`ratio()` returns `null` when the denominator is absent or zero, and `null` renders as `—`. A
+collection rate over no billed amount is undefined, not zero percent.
+
+**M7. Currency is carried once per surface.**
+The currency symbol is stated by the panel, the card header, or the topmost axis tick — not repeated
+down every row or tick. Repeating a currency code five times is five copies of a fact the reader
+learned from the first one.
+
+## Status and lifecycle
+
+**S1. Status presentation has one source of truth.**
+`lib/ui/status.ts` owns every label and tone. Nothing at a call site decides a status colour.
+*Fails if:* a component contains a status string literal next to a colour decision.
+
+**S2. Every schema enum member is covered, and coverage is enforced by test.**
+`tests/status_test.ts` reads `schema.prisma` and asserts each member of `InvoiceStatus`, `RunStatus`,
+`RunItemStatus`, `PaymentStatus`, `PaymentAttemptOutcome`, `CreditNoteStatus` and
+`WebhookEventStatus` has a presentation. Adding an enum member fails the suite until the UI covers
+it. An unrecognised status renders in the neutral tone with its raw value as the label — it surfaces,
+it does not vanish.
+
+**S3. In-flight never relies on colour alone.**
+`COMPUTING`, `ISSUING`, `RETRYING` and `DECLINED_SOFT` are marked `live` and carry a pulsing marker
+in addition to their tone, because in-flight and issued share a hue family. Colour is never the only
+channel for state.
+
+**S4. Derived states are declared as derived.**
+Part-paid and partially-refunded are computed from applied payments and credit notes, not stored.
+They carry `derived: true` so a reader knows the database did not say so.
+
+**S5. A failed read is data, not an exception.**
+An authoritative read that fails yields `unavailable` and renders a labelled frame. It never renders
+five zeros, and it never throws into the page. Degrade the expensive half of a surface, never the
+cheap one.
+
+## Composition and card anatomy
+
+**C1. One card grammar, five bands.**
+header (glyph + title + optional info) · action affordance top-right (pill dropdown **or** outline
+button, never both) · hero metric + delta chip · body visualisation · footer strip or full-width CTA.
+Every composed widget obeys it, which is what makes a page read as one system.
+
+**C2. The hero number dominates.**
+The hero metric is roughly 3× the label, bold, tabular. Everything else on the card is quiet. A card
+with no single answer to give has no hero — the audit trail carries no headline figure, because its
+whole content is the evidence and a big number on top would be decoration.
+
+**C3. The delta chip is one component.**
+Rounded pill, tinted background, directional glyph, signed value, semantic colour. Every
+"up/down vs last period" in the product is this component. Not a re-styled badge.
+
+**C4. Segmented controls select by filling, not by bordering.**
+Range selection is a segmented control whose selected cell is a filled pill. Unselected cells are
+transparent with hairline dividers. A selected state that only changes a border is rejected.
+
+**C5. Equal-width footer columns, separated by hairlines.**
+A footer strip is N equal columns of label + value, divided by hairline rules, never by gaps alone.
+
+**C6. Legends are inline dot + label.**
+Never a boxed key, never a bordered legend panel.
+
+## Charts
+
+**H1. Charts are hand-authored SVG over tokens. No charting library.**
+Geometry is computed in TypeScript and emitted as SVG. No dependency renders a chart.
+
+**H2. A chart never formats a value.**
+Values arrive preformatted as strings. A chart component takes `label: string`, never a number it
+would have to format. Currency and units are the caller's decision.
+
+**H3. Series colours come from the fixed `--ns-series-1..6` cycle.**
+A series keeps its colour across renders and across routes because the cycle is keyed by index, not
+by data order. Never assign colour by value, and never let a sort re-colour a series.
+
+**H4. Hover is CSS, not JS.**
+Readouts, crosshairs and point markers are CSS `:hover` on the SVG group. No hydration cost, no
+first-paint mismatch. A hover that needs a `useState` is rejected.
+
+**H5. Comparison is a second translucent layer, never a second axis.**
+A comparison period is the same geometry at reduced opacity (`color-mix(...transparent)`), overlaid.
+Two axes on one plot is rejected.
+
+**H6. Chart chrome is minimal.**
+No plot border, faint or absent gridlines (`--ns-chart-grid`), axis labels only where they earn
+their place, and currency carried on the topmost tick only.
+
+**H7. A chart with no data renders a labelled empty frame.**
+Not a flat line at zero, and not a zero axis. "No usage recorded in this period" is a different
+statement from "usage was zero", and the chart must make it.
+
+## Data, density and absence
+
+**D1. Dense surfaces declare their geometry once in TypeScript.**
+Column widths, row heights and widget names live in one `as const` declaration that the component,
+its skeleton and its CSS all consume. Duplicating a width in two stylesheets is a defect.
+
+**D2. A wide audit trail scrolls inside its own panel.**
+It never sizes the page. Hundreds of rows are contained.
+
+**D3. Recency first in a trail.**
+The newest event leads. Leading with any other column makes the reader scan sideways for the one
+fact that orders the table.
+
+**D4. Every reachable state is designed.**
+draft · issued · paid · part-paid · failed · retrying · refunded · partly refunded · voided ·
+in-flight · empty · loading · permission-denied. A component that only renders the happy path is
+unfinished, and `permission-denied` is a state, not an error page.
+
+**D5. Filters are local component state, never query keys.**
+A filter is a projection over data already on the page. No filter combination may fragment a warm
+cache entry. The sentinel for "no filter" is `'all'`, never `''` — an empty string is the falsy
+value that silently turns an exact key into a prefix.
+
+## Interaction and islands
+
+**I1. Hydration is earned, not assumed.**
+An island exists because interaction requires it. Static render is the default. The boundary is two
+lines: an island wrapper that sets up the client runtime and an inner component that does the work.
+Inner components never import server-only modules.
+
+**I2. Data arrives as props.**
+Islands do not fetch what the route already loaded. Seeds come from the loader; live data overrides
+the seed once it materialises (`live.length ? live : seed`).
+
+**I3. No success toast on an in-place action.**
+The pressed state is the confirmation. Toasts are reserved for outcomes the user cannot see.
+
+**I4. Cross-island coordination is a module-level signal.**
+Not a context provider, not an event bus.
+
+## Language
+
+**L1. Destructive actions use Verb + Noun.**
+"Void invoice", "Retry payment", "Exclude item". Never `Confirm`, never `OK`, never a bare verb. The
+button says what it will do to what.
+
+**L2. State is a past participle; process is a gerund.**
+An invoice is *issued*; a run is *issuing*. Never `Invoice issued successfully` — the row already
+shows it.
+
+**L3. An error names the entity and the remedy.**
+"Payment declined by issuer — retry or update the card." Never "Something went wrong", never a bare
+status code.
+
+**L4. Labels are human, never enum members.**
+`UNCOLLECTIBLE` renders "Uncollectible"; `DECLINED_SOFT` renders "Soft decline". Enforced by test.
+
+## Theme and CSS discipline
+
+**T1. `assets/tokens.json` is the source; `tokens.css` is generated from it.**
+Both are edited together and never diverge. Every colour, radius, space, shadow and duration used by
+a component is a `--ns-*` token.
+
+**T2. No raw colour literal outside the token files.**
+No hex, no `rgb()`, no `rgba()` in `assets/ui/**` or `assets/blocks/**`. Derived states use
+`color-mix()`, never a new literal.
+
+**T3. No component branches on theme.**
+Light and dark are role overrides under `[data-theme='dark']` only. A component that reads the
+current theme is a defect.
+
+**T4. Customize through the seams, in this order.**
+(1) a `data-*` attribute the component already emits; (2) a `class` prop merged last by `cn()`;
+(3) a per-surface block file imported *after* the component file with the cascade order commented.
+
+**T5. Never fork a component, never a parallel stylesheet, no `!important`.**
+A second copy of a component to change one thing is rejected. Overrides ride the documented seams.
+
+**T6. Every new component owns its stylesheet.**
+One file per component under `assets/ui/` (primitive) or `assets/blocks/` (composed surface),
+imported from `assets/styles.css`. A component with no stylesheet entry is unreachable.
+
+## Registration
+
+**R1. A component missing from the barrel is invisible.**
+Every component is exported from `components/ui/mod.ts` and registered in
+`routes/(design)/design/(_shared)/registry.ts`, with a demo in `components-view.tsx`. Unregistered
+work does not exist.
+
+**R2. Gallery counts and ramp orders are read from the manifest, never typed by hand.**
+`RAMP_ORDER` in `(_shared)/tokens.ts` must match the real ramp names in `tokens.json` or a ramp
+silently vanishes from the gallery.
+
+---
+
+# Patterns we refuse to ship
+
+These are the generated-design tells. Each is refused on sight, with the reason.
+
+1. **A generic dashboard re-skinned.** Grid of four stat cards, a bar chart, a recent-activity
+   table — arranged the same way in every product. Refused because nothing in it could only exist
+   for billing.
+2. **Emoji as iconography.** `✅ ❌ ⚠️ 💰` in place of drawn glyphs. Refused: they are font-dependent,
+   unthemeable, and they silently change colour across platforms. Icons are inline SVG or a token-
+   coloured glyph from one set.
+3. **Purple-blue gradient accents with a generic sans.** The default SaaS palette. Refused: this
+   product's identity is paper/ink/ledger-green/brass, and a gradient is not a design decision.
+4. **Rounded-everything and uniform elevation.** Every surface the same radius and the same soft
+   shadow, so nothing is structural. Refused: radius and elevation encode containment.
+5. **The centred empty state with a big illustration.** Refused in dense operational surfaces: an
+   audit trail that is empty says so in one line inside its own frame, and does not borrow a hero.
+6. **A charting dependency.** Refused: see H1. It also drags its own colours in, which breaks T2.
+7. **A modal to confirm a modal.** Refused: see L1 — the button names the action instead.
+8. **Placeholder copy and lorem.** Refused: every demo string in the gallery is a real Ledgerline
+   value — a real invoice number, a real plan name, a real decline reason.
+9. **`0.00` where the truth is "not measured".** Refused: see M1. In billing this is correctness.
+10. **A status colour decided at the call site.** Refused: see S1.
+11. **Everything interactive.** Refused: see I1. A surface that hydrates to render text is paying a
+    cost for nothing.
+12. **Responsive by shrinking alone.** Refused: dense tables collapse into labelled cells
+    (`responsive-table`), they do not shrink to illegibility.

